# Valley Floodcaller: "You may cast noncreature spells as though they had flash" (CR 307.5, 702.8). In Bot2's turn 2 Bot1
# casts Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber as its left door, Unholy Annex: the spell is that door alone (CR 709.3a), an
# enchantment. The ruling: the permission "has no effect on abilities that you can activate 'any time you could cast a
# sorcery'", nor on the unlock of a door, a special action at sorcery timing (CR 709.5e): in Bot2's turn 4, with the
# {3}{B}{B} for Ritual Chamber untapped, the unlock is refused, and in Bot1's own turn 5 it is taken - the positive
# control - and makes the 6/6 Demon. Unholy Annex's end-step trigger in turn 3, with no Demon yet, costs Bot1 2 life.

